@node Overview
@chapter Overview

arise (@emph{Gentoo Manager}) is an experimental statically-linked Go control
plane that aims to provide compatible workflows for
@command{emerge}, @command{eix}, @command{equery}, @command{quickpkg},
@command{perl-cleaner}, @command{python-updater}, @command{dispatch-conf},
@command{env-update}, @command{revdep-rebuild}, and @command{eselect news}.

It stores package metadata in a BadgerDB key-value store and operates directly
against the Gentoo repository tree and VDB, without depending on Python or
Bash for core operations. Build phases that require shell scripts execute via
@code{os/exec} to the appropriate build tools.

The project priorities are correctness, usefulness, performance, and
reliability. Repair planning is intended to derive and verify the complete
ordered closure needed to recover an old or damaged installation, rather than
requiring the administrator to widen hand-selected @option{--oneshot
--nodeps} batches by trial and error. Indexed immutable state and Go
concurrency reduce control-plane latency without weakening deterministic
results or whole-state verification. Unusual but valid Gentoo configurations,
including split-usr systems, remain compatibility inputs.

@table @emph
@item Pure Go and static linking
@code{CGO_ENABLED=0}. The Arise control plane has no runtime dependency on
Python or shared libraries. Package execution still invokes the native Bash
and build tools required by Gentoo ebuild semantics.

@item Optional integrations
Enhancements that introduce an additional Arise runtime dependency require a
functional baseline fallback and an explicit Gentoo USE flag. Bubblewrap and
filesystem snapshot providers are optional strengthening layers, not gates for
ordinary control-plane or Portage-compatible behavior.

@item Filesystem is sovereign
The database is an acceleration layer. The filesystem (ebuild tree, VDB) is
the authoritative source of truth.

@item Pragmatic fallback
Build phases (configure, make, install) shell out to the native tools.
Core logic (resolution, metadata, auditing) is pure Go.

@item Self-healing
Remains operational even when system Python or portage libraries are broken.
@end table

Live-root install, update, reinstall, and uninstall execute directly after a
verified plan. Explicit install targets are selected into world unless
@option{--oneshot} is set. Saved plans remain available for optional
state-bound review and deferred execution. Source transactions use isolated
phase workers, durable logs, operation locking, package journals, and resumable
dependency-aware scheduling. Arise is not yet a general Portage replacement.
Live package management remains experimental and the overlay release is
testing-keyworded for @code{~amd64}; keep Portage installed as the reference and
recovery implementation. Depclean and broader maintenance mutation remain
unavailable until their complete transaction and recovery contracts pass.

@node Quick Start
@chapter Quick Start

@example
# Build from source
$ CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -ldflags="-s -w" -o arise ./cmd/arise/

# Sync the Gentoo repository
$ arise --repo-url https://anongit.gentoo.org/git/repo/gentoo.git sync

# Index metadata for fast queries
$ arise index

# Search packages
$ arise search gcc
$ arise search --installed --category dev-lang
$ arise search --versions --json python

# Installed package inspection
$ arise installed --owner /usr/bin/gcc
$ arise installed --contents sys-devel/gcc
$ arise installed --size sys-devel/gcc
$ arise installed --uses sys-devel/gcc
$ arise installed --check sys-devel/gcc
$ arise query --ebuild sys-devel/gcc

# Resolve an install without mutation
$ arise --pretend install app-editors/vim

# Resolve a world update without mutation
$ arise --pretend update

# Audit for outdated packages
$ arise audit python
$ arise audit perl
@end example

@node Invocation
@chapter Invocation Syntax

@example
arise [@var{global-flags}] @var{command} [@var{args}@dots{}]
@end example

Global flags must precede the command name. Package and search flags
follow the command.

@table @asis
@item @option{-db @var{path}}
Database path. Default: @file{/var/lib/arise/data}.
@item @option{-repo @var{path}}
Repository path. Default: @file{/var/db/repos/gentoo}.
@item @option{-repo-url @var{url}}
Remote repository URL for sync.
@end table

