@node Package Management
@section Package Management

@table @command
@item install [flags] @var{atoms@dots{}}
Resolve, build, install, and select one or more packages. Use
@option{--oneshot} to suppress world selection. @option{--pretend} displays the
verified plan without mutation; @option{--preflight-only} additionally validates
each planned recipe and execution policy without running build tools.
Manifest-verified @option{--fetchonly} is a bounded non-mutation operation.

@item update [flags] [@var{atoms@dots{}}]
Resolve and execute updates, defaulting to @code{@@world}.

@item uninstall @var{atoms@dots{}}
Verify and execute journaled package removal. Use @option{--pretend} for a
read-only proposal.

@item depclean [flags]
Propose orphan removal without mutation.

@item prune [flags]
Propose old-version removal without mutation.

@item deselect @var{atom}
Remove a package from @@world without uninstalling.

@item select @var{atom}
Add exactly one installed package atom to @@world using locked, state-bound
world-file mutation.

@item recover status
List durable package journals and their state.

@item recover rollback @var{id}
Roll back one active journal while holding the VDB mutation lock. Use
@option{--all-active} in place of @var{id} to recover every active journal.

@item recover inspect-set @var{path}
Verify a complete recovery set, display reverse capture order, and report the
exact approval digest required when configuration or repository state drifted.

@item recover restore-set @var{path}
Restore every verified artifact through journaled package merges while holding
the VDB lock. Drift requires
@option{--approve-recovery-drift-sha256} with the digest reported by
@code{inspect-set}.

@item recover verify-set @var{path}
Mark a pending recovery set verified only after the kernel reports a different
boot identity from the one recorded when the set was captured.

@item recover prune-sets @var{keep}
Retain the newest requested number of verified recovery sets. Every non-verified
or unreadable set is preserved.
@end table

@node Query and Information
@section Query and Information

@table @command
@item search [flags] [@var{query}]
Search the package database with eix-style filtering.
See @ref{Search Filters} for all available search flags.

@item installed [@var{inspection-option}] [@var{argument}]
List or inspect installed packages. Versionless line output is the default.
Inspection options cover ownership, contents, USE flags, installed size,
integrity, atom matching, presence, and best installed versions.

@item query [@var{query-option}] @var{atom}
Query indexed repository, binary-package, or installed metadata. It can report
best-visible versions, metadata keys, virtual expansion, and ebuild paths.
For repository metadata, a versioned atom inspects its matching indexed
candidate even when mask or keyword policy makes that candidate invisible;
an unversioned atom selects the best visible candidate.

@item state @var{subcommand}
Emit deterministic available or installed package state used by parity,
snapshot, and differential workflows.

@item info [@var{information-option}] [@var{argument}]
Display system, repository, path, eclass, license, protected-configuration,
preserved-library, and color information.

@item inspect [--json] [--strict] [--locked] [--target-kernel=@var{release}] @var{atom}
Explain installed and prospective package state from one stabilized snapshot.
The report includes visibility and USE provenance, dependency and reverse
dependency context, kernel requirements, out-of-tree module rebuild state, and
typed incomplete-evidence diagnostics. The default lockless mode works for
unprivileged users and requires two agreeing observations. @option{--locked}
also observes Portage locks, while @option{--strict} rejects partial evidence.
JSON output uses the @code{arise.package-inspect.v1} contract.
@end table

@subheading Native Package Query Examples

Arise is a self-contained alternative that works alongside @command{emerge},
@command{eix}, @command{equery}, @command{portageq}, and the @command{q} tools.
It neither replaces those programs nor copies their command names. Default
line-oriented output, package atoms, exit statuses, and Portage paths remain
suitable for mixed shell pipelines. Requiring another package tool to diagnose
Arise package state or a failed Arise operation identifies missing Arise
diagnostic surface.

@example
# Installed matches, presence, and best installed version
$ arise installed --match '>=llvm-core/clang-19'
$ arise installed --has llvm-core/clang
$ arise installed --best llvm-core/clang

# Installed files, owners, USE state, size, and integrity
$ arise installed --contents llvm-core/clang
$ arise installed --owner /usr/bin/clang
$ arise installed --uses llvm-core/clang
$ arise installed --size llvm-core/clang
$ arise installed --check llvm-core/clang

# Repository, binary-package, and installed metadata
$ arise query --best-visible llvm-core/clang
$ arise query --best-visible --type=binary llvm-core/clang
$ arise query --metadata=SLOT,KEYWORDS llvm-core/clang
$ arise query --metadata=KEYWORDS,RDEPEND '=dev-python/sphinx-9.1.0-r1'
$ arise query --expand-virtual virtual/libc
$ arise query --ebuild llvm-core/clang

# Unified package-state explanation
$ arise inspect llvm-core/clang
$ arise inspect --target-kernel="$(uname -r)" sys-fs/zfs-kmod
$ arise inspect --json dev-python/sphinx

# Portage configuration and repository paths
$ arise info --value DISTDIR PKGDIR
$ arise info --repositories
$ arise info --repo-path gentoo
$ arise info --eclasses gentoo
$ arise info --license-path gentoo GPL-2
$ arise info --preserved-libs
$ arise info --is-protected /etc/hosts

# Maintainer discovery and machine-readable state
$ arise search --search-maintainer maintainer@@gentoo.org
$ arise search --search-orphaned
$ arise state json
@end example

Batch forms accept multiple atoms, paths, repositories, or variables where
shown by @command{arise @var{command} --help}. The complete reference-tool
equivalence table is maintained in @file{docs/tool-equivalents.md} in the
source distribution.

@node System Maintenance
@section System Maintenance

@table @command
@item sync [@var{repository}...]
Synchronize all configured repositories, or only the repositories named as
arguments, via git (primary) or rsync (fallback), then atomically publish the
refreshed resolver index. Git repositories whose fetched branch has not
changed are left untouched. The default output summarizes package/version-set
changes with eix-style tags; @option{-v} includes transport and per-ebuild
diagnostics. Independent repositories synchronize concurrently, while final
reports retain configured order. Per-repository @option{clone-depth} and
@option{sync-depth} values are read from @file{repos.conf}; the default is 1,
and 0 requests full history. Success means both stages completed.

@item index
Rebuild the BadgerDB metadata database from the ebuild tree.

@item audit @var{python|perl} [--fix]
Audit installed packages for outdated Python or Perl site-packages paths.
@option{--fix --pretend} lists the affected rebuild set. Non-pretend
@option{--fix} remains gated and fails explicitly.

@item perl-cleaner --modules|--allmodules|--libperl|--all|--reallyall
Audit and repair installed Perl modules and libperl consumers from VDB
metadata without requiring a working Perl interpreter or Portage Python
runtime. The familiar mode distinctions are preserved. Repair targets use the
verified resolver, final state is re-audited, known generated leftovers are
journaled, and unknown leftovers are reported. @option{--resume} restores the
integrity-bound cleaner mode, ABI evidence, targets, and leftover policy while
the executor resumes remaining packages. @option{--skipfirst} is supported when
saved package progress exists.

@item python-cleaner --check|--pretend|--fix|--resume
Inventory Python transitions from effective target policy, python-exec
preference, installed slots, package USE metadata, owned paths, libpython
linkage, root-confined shebangs, and unowned obsolete site-packages. Pretend
mode isolates dependency-connected repair cohorts, pins viable installed
versions, reports unavailable historical ebuilds, resolves each cohort, and
shows the ordered validation, preference-switch, and removal stages.
@option{--fix} applies checkpointed cohorts with a fresh inventory after each
transaction, probes policy interpreters and rebuilt native extensions, and
atomically publishes python-exec preference only after validation.
@option{--resume} restores integrity-bound recovery state. Unavailable ebuilds
block preference switching. The workflow does not yet remove interpreters or
orphan files.

@item maintain world --check|--fix
Check the selected world set against installed packages and every configured
repository. Check mode supports deterministic text and versioned JSON. Fix
mode requires a state-bound approved plan, revalidates beneath the Portage
world lock, and atomically preserves file mode and ownership.

@item maintain moveinst --check|--fix
Check or apply ordered repository package moves to installed VDB identities,
slots, and dependency metadata. Fix mode locks and revalidates the VDB and
commits through a rollback journal.

@item maintain merges --check|--fix|--purge
Audit interrupted @code{-MERGING-} VDB entries and Portage failed-merge
tracking. Fix mode journals confined cleanup, rebuilds exact atoms through
Arise, and retains tracking when rebuilding fails. Purge removes only tracking.

@item maintain resume --check|--fix
Audit or transactionally clear Arise resume state and Portage's @code{resume}
and @code{resume_backup} mtimedb records while preserving unrelated keys.
@code{cleanresume} is accepted as an alias.

@item bug-report [--output @var{directory}]
Create private, reviewable Markdown and versioned JSON diagnostics without
uploading anything. @option{--archive} adds a deterministic @file{.tar.zst}
export. Collection is bounded and default-deny, and redacts local identity,
credentials, tokens, proxy values, and private URL components.

@item preserved-rebuild [flags]
Scan for broken shared library links and rebuild affected packages.

@item revdep-rebuild [flags]
Full reverse dependency scan for broken ELF dependencies.

@item bench
Run Arise's built-in microbenchmark report. Correctness-gated external
comparisons use the dedicated performance harness.
@end table

@node Configuration
@section Configuration

@table @command
@item dispatch-conf
Interactively review and merge recursive CONFIG_PROTECT updates with archives
and conf-update hooks. This is a usable replacement workflow with safe
three-way premerge, confined atomic archives, mixed-file diffs, and
interruption-aware processing. Session rollback/recovery and broader
command-level differential parity remain under development.

@item env-update
Regenerate @file{/etc/profile.env} and @file{/etc/csh.env}.

@item ldconfig
Update the shared library linker cache.

@item config @var{atom}
Run the @code{pkg_config} phase.

@item news list
List Gentoo news items (GLEP 42) with stable selection numbers and unread
status.

@item news read @var{number}|all
Mark one numbered news item, or every item, as read.

@item news display @var{number}
Display one numbered news item and mark it read.
@end table

@node Binary Packages
@section Binary Packages

@table @command
@item quickpkg [@option{--gpkg}] @var{atom}
Create a machine-bound recovery artifact by default. @option{--gpkg} writes a
zstd-compressed GLEP 78 package readable by current Portage, containing the
installed paths recorded by CONTENTS and complete VDB metadata.
@end table

@node Search Filters
@chapter Search Filters

The @command{search} command supports eix-compatible filtering with the
following flags:

@table @option
@item --name @var{pkg}
Filter by package name.
@item --category @var{cat}
Filter by category.
@item --slot @var{slot}
Filter by SLOT.
@item --use @var{flags}
USE flag filter (leading @code{+} required, @code{-} excluded).
@item --keywords @var{kw}
Filter by KEYWORDS content.
@item --license @var{lic}
Filter by LICENSE.
@item --desc
Search in descriptions.
@item --installed
Only show installed packages.
@item --exact
Exact match instead of substring.
@item --regex
Treat patterns as regular expressions.
@item --stable
Only stable-keyworded packages.
@item --testing
Only testing-keyworded packages.
@item --sort @var{order}
Sort by @code{category}, @code{name}, @code{version}, or @code{slot}.
@item --versions
Show all available versions.
@item --format @var{fmt}
Custom output format with template variables.
@item --print @var{fields}
Print specific fields (space-separated).
@item --json
JSON output.
@item --brief
Single-line output.
@item --compact
Compact output.
@item --only-names
Output only package names.
@item --count-only
Output only result count.
@item --and
Combine queries with AND logic.
@item --not @var{pattern}
Exclude packages matching pattern.
@item --world
Only @@world packages.
@item --system
Only @@system packages.
@item --depends-on @var{atom}
Packages that depend on atom.
@item --required-by @var{atom}
Packages required by atom.
@item --has-use @var{flag}
Packages with this USE flag available.
@item --has-version @var{pat}
Packages with version matching glob.
@item --care
Show packages needing attention.
@item --overflow
Only packages with masked keywords.
@item --masked
Only masked packages.
@item --duplicates
Show all versions of each package.
@item --dump
Dump in eix-compatible format.
@end table

@node Package Flags
@chapter Package Flags

Flags available for @command{install}, @command{update}, and @command{depclean}:

@table @option
@item -1, --oneshot
Install without adding to @@world.
@item -O, --nodeps
Skip dependency resolution.
@item -o, --onlydeps
Only install dependencies.
@item -e, --emptytree
Rebuild as if nothing is installed.
@item -D, --deep
Full dependency tree.
@item -u, --update
Update to best version.
@item -N, --newuse
Rebuild on USE changes.
@item -p, --pretend
Dry run.
@item -a, --ask
Prompt before acting.
@item -q, --quiet
Minimal output.
@item -v, --verbose
Verbose output.
@item --debug
Show resolver stage timings and the candidate decision ledger. These
diagnostics are separate from verbose package and USE details.
@item -t, --tree
Dependency tree display.
@item -j @var{N}, --jobs @var{N}
Parallel jobs.
@item -k, --usepkg
Use binary packages.
@item -K, --usepkgonly
Only binary packages.
@item -b, --buildpkg
Build deterministic GPKG binary packages in PKGDIR and install them normally.
@item -B, --buildpkgonly
Build deterministic GPKG binary packages in PKGDIR without modifying ROOT.
@item -f, --fetchonly
Only fetch sources.
@item --backtrack @var{N}
Maximum backtracking decisions (default 20).
@item --resolver-timeout @var{duration}
Wall-clock resolver deadline (default @code{5m}). @code{0} disables the
deadline without changing the independent backtrack ceiling.
@item --approve-plan-sha256 @var{digest}
Optionally require the current plan to match this canonical verified-plan
digest, including its package state and policy fingerprint.
@item --save-plan @var{path-or-name}
Save the complete generated JSON plan for later inspection and approval.
@item --approve-plan @var{path-or-name}
Optionally require execution to match an exact saved plan after current state
and policy are revalidated.
@item --preflight-only
Validate every planned package without fetching, building, or mutating.
@item --plan-dir @var{path}
Directory used for named saved plans.
@item --journal-dir @var{path}
Directory containing durable package transaction journals.
@item --resume-file @var{path}
Path containing resumable package-action state.
@item --work-dir @var{path}
Package build and transaction workspace.
@item --fetch-jobs @var{N}
Concurrent source fetch and verification jobs.
@item --show-estimates
Show historical per-package and serial-total merge-time estimates. Estimates
are advisory and do not affect plan authorization or scheduling.
@item --complete-graph
Rebuild reverse deps.
@item --keep-going
Continue on errors.
@item --reinstall
Force reinstall.
@item --changed-use
Reinstall on USE changes.
@item --changed-deps
Reinstall on DEPEND changes.
@item --noreplace
Skip same version.
@item --exclude @var{pkg}
Exclude package (repeatable).
@item --resume
Resume last operation.
@item --skipfirst
Skip first in resume.
@item --autounmask-write
Write unmask entries.
@item --color y|n
Colored output.
@item --unordered-display
Unsorted display.
@item --load-average @var{LOAD}
Pause above load threshold.
@item --getbinpkg
Download the resolved dependency closure from configured Packages-indexed
binhosts and use compatible binaries with source fallback.
@item --getbinpkgonly
Download the resolved dependency closure from configured Packages-indexed
binhosts and require compatible binaries for the complete plan.
@item --binpkg-respect-use
USE-aware binpkg selection.
@item --with-bdeps y|n|auto
BDEPEND handling.
@item --ignore-built-slot-operator-deps y|n
Ignore slot operator rebuilds.
@end table

@node Configuration Files
@chapter Configuration Files

@table @file
@item /etc/portage/make.conf
Global system configuration (CHOST, CFLAGS, USE, MAKEOPTS, FEATURES,
ACCEPT_KEYWORDS, ACCEPT_LICENSE, PORTAGE_BINHOST).

@item /etc/portage/package.use[/]
Per-package USE flag overrides. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords[/]
Per-package keyword overrides. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.license[/]
Per-package license acceptance. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.mask[/]
Masked packages (prevent installation). May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.unmask[/]
Override masks for specific packages. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.env[/]
Per-package environment file assignments. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/profile/package.provided
User-provided virtual packages.

@item /etc/portage/make.profile
Symlink to the active Gentoo profile.

@item /var/lib/portage/world
User-requested package list (@@world set).

@item /var/db/repos/gentoo/
Gentoo repository tree.

@item /var/db/pkg/
VDB: installed package database.

@item /var/cache/binpkgs/
Binary package cache.

@item /var/tmp/arise/
Temporary build directory.

@item /var/tmp/arise/resume
Resume state for interrupted operations.
@end table

@node Extending arise
@chapter Extending arise

arise's internal packages are organized by concern:

@table @file
@item internal/atom
Gentoo atom parser. Handles @code{>=cat/pkg-1.0:slot=[use]} syntax.

@item internal/depstring
DEPEND/RDEPEND string parser. Handles @code{||}, @code{use?}, @code{!},
@code{^^}, nested groups, slot constraints.

@item internal/ebuild
Ebuild file parser. Extracts EAPI, inherit, variables, phase functions.

@item internal/eclass
Eclass loader. Resolves inherit chains, merges variables and exported functions.

@item internal/metadata
md5-cache parser. PackageMetadata struct with EAPI 8+ fields.

@item internal/graph
Dependency graph builder. Queries BadgerDB and walks the ebuild tree.

@item internal/resolve
Backtracking dependency solver. USE, keyword, license, mask awareness.

@item internal/rebuild
Source build pipeline: verified fetch -> isolated phase execution -> image
validation -> journaled payload/VDB transaction -> lifecycle finalization.
Saved-plan approval is optional; every mutation still uses state verification,
operation locking, journaling, rollback, and lifecycle finalization.

@item internal/portage
Configuration parser. make.conf, package.use, package.accept_keywords, etc.

@item internal/profile
Profile inheritance chain parser. load parent chains, merge settings.

@item internal/binpkg
XPAK binary package read/write with USE compatibility checking.

@item internal/search
eix-style package search with 30+ filter options.

@item internal/packagequery
Package query: belongs, files, uses, size, check, which, list.
@end table

Coverage varies by subsystem. The maintained test lanes include unit,
adversarial, fuzz, race, differential and disposable-root integration tests;
the punch list records the remaining acceptance gates.

